# Preset: cg27a_rtxw_pass1 - cg27a_rtxt_pass1 + REAL-TEXT REPLAY THROUGH THE WIKIPEDIA SLOT (inf_distill_rtx_slot 1; one change): the forgetting fix
# (cg27a_rtxt: forgetting +0.077 vs +0.026; Gutenberg +0.224). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rtxt_pass1 - cg27a_rtx16_pass1 + TITLE FOR PRONOUN (inf_distill_rtx_title 1; one change): pronoun-led replayed real sentences replayed
# with the document's title for the pronoun. Named sentences confirm the real-text result to visit 10. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rtx16_pass1 - cg27a_rtx_pass1 with four times the real-text replay (inf_distill_rtx 16; one change). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rtx_pass1 - cg27a_replay_pass1 + REAL-TEXT REPLAY of half the benchmark documents as plain text, NO view alignment
# (inf_distill_rtx 4, inf_distill_rtx_align 0; one change: replay is the single cause). The test: real-text recall from the weights, replayed vs control documents. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_replay_pass1 - cg27a_align_pass1 + SOURCE REPLAY (inf_distill_replay 4; ONE model change): the stored source sentences of the
# question pool's facts and of the never-asked control fifth replayed as plain text with every question-row step. The test: the trunk
# completes control facts' own sentences (cg27a_align 0.00) and then answers them in the test wordings (never asked). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_align_pass1 - cg27a_rwclean_pass1 + VIEW ALIGNMENT (inf_distill_align 0.5; ONE model change, after LLM-JEPA): each taught
# question row's state at the answer is pulled toward the state where the fact's own source sentence predicts the answer (a stop-gradient
# target). The test is the never-taught CONTROL fifth in the test wordings (facts the trunk only READ). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rwclean_pass1 - cg27a_chunk_pass1 + the clean step-4 control (inf_rw_nosleep 1: the rule world's two-hop pairs are never
# concluded by the sleep layer, so composites reach the trunk only through the relational module's write). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_chunk_pass1 - cg27a_relwrite_pass1 (step 4, the same one model change) + the FAST SEQUENCE CHANNEL READER as readouts
# (inf_reader_chunk 1: a separate evidence record scored against the gold relations; the relational module on real text). The step-4 readout
# now also reports recall with the closed-form edits subtracted. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_relwrite_pass1 - cg27a_relmod_pass1 (with the fixed relational module) + STEP 4: its verified conclusions WRITTEN into the
# distillation question pool (inf_distill_relmod_write 1; ONE model change). The test: the trunk recalls composite facts never planted. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_relmod_pass1 - cg27a_rag_pass1 + the RELATIONAL MODULE readout (inf_distill_relmod 1500; step 3 of the rule test): rules discovered
# from the reader's facts against a shuffled null and a functional check, typed conclusions proposed and scored, nothing written. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rag_pass1 - the new defaults (= cg27a_distillcap_pass1, plus the RULE WORLD) + retrieval-augmented answers with cited sources,
# latent chaining and operator algebra on the rule world (readouts; no model change). Seed 4 (the notebook's SEED line must be 4).
# Preset: cg27a_distillcap_pass1 - cg27a_distillm_pass1 with the question pool beyond the name memory's cap (inf_distill_pool_max 2000; ONE model change),
# the ever-taught ledger readout and the store-write stage memory marks. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_distillm_pass1 - cg27a_distillw_pass1 with the question rows restricted to the blocks' mlp_out weights (ONE model change), the
# Gaussian drift readout, per-phase GPU peaks and cache release, memory guard 0.6. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_distillw_pass1 - cg27a_carry_pass1 + INTERLEAVED DISTILLATION (inf_distill_wake 0.25: 4 question rows about stored facts in every
# real-text training step, same backward and optimiser; a fifth of the facts never taught). The sleep burst (inf_distill) stays off. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_carry_pass1 - cg27a_readouts_pass1 + CARRY THE SUBJECT (inf_carry 0.1: an auxiliary loss teaching the trunk to keep the latest
# name readable at the bytes after it; the test is the [SLOT CARRIES THE SUBJECT?] readout every third sleep). Seed 4, as the run without it.
# Preset: cg27a_readouts_pass1 - the current build (cg27a, self-contrast on) with every 9 Nov readout: answer-slot gates, system-written question forms
# in the shadow edits, ROME-style fit diagnostic, latent judge hard controls, sticky routing, sleep phases, ceiling tests last. Seed 3: a third seed.
# Preset: cg27a_pass1 - cg27a for pass 1 only (10 visits, about 2 hours; the end-of-run readouts come after visit 10). cg27a = cg26z (closed loop with hints, the store reads the text) + the write side: conclusions in several wordings, competitor contrast, information-weighted answer bytes, closed-form edits on three wordings (branch cg27a)
# The JEPA index trains its own small text encoder on the stored sentences each sleep and reports retrieval,
# one-hop with the retrieved sentence in context and two-hop by retrieval; cg26u adds two more encoder arms
# (C: InfoNCE; G: names masked, a generic trace), routing of each visit by bytes and by JEPA codes, and where
# the replay teacher signal sits by byte class. All readouts: the trunk and the router are not changed by them.
# Build: the platypus package (python -m platypus).
# Clean evaluation is the build's default: oracle options off (REM subjects
# not drawn from the planted probe facts, dream cues not chosen by benchmark
# gold entities, JEPA batches not balanced by the planted label), held-out
# probe wordings with the bridge among the candidates and no slot given,
# schema fit measured with its own prompt. PLATYPUS_CLEAN=0 restores cg26p.

PRESET_BUILD=platypus
PRESET_SEED=4

PLATYPUS_CLEAN=1

# Conduit hints in the closed-loop passes (true bytes given to the generator).
# 1 = as cg26p; 0 = none (the strict closed loop; GPU cg26w: 0.87-0.99 of replay rebuilt exactly).
PLATYPUS_HINTS=1

# Closed-form edits (re-solve every sleep). 0 turns them off.
PLATYPUS_CF=1

# Sleep schedule: adaptive (default since cg26n) or fixed.
PLATYPUS_SLEEP=adaptive

PLATYPUS_DREAMS=jepa
PLATYPUS_RULEFREE=1
PLATYPUS_ROUTEFIX=1
PLATYPUS_PASSES=1
PILE_CACHE=pile_cache
FLA_AUTO_INSTALL=1

# PLATYPUS_SLOTS=N would let the router open up to N slots (more than the
# number of domains); locally every revisit then went to a new slot, so the
# cap stays until the router recognises revisits by itself.

# Function timer: 1 prints the seconds spent in each sleep, readout and
# diagnostic function after every visit and for the whole run (adds a GPU
# synchronisation per call, so a little slower). Off by default.
PLATYPUS_FNTIME=0

# The JEPA index, routing and byte-class readout options.
LAB_OVR_FILE=configs/presets/cg27a_rtxw.overrides.json
